{"skill":{"slug":"agent-analytics","displayName":"agent-analytics"},"version":{"version":"4.0.37","createdAt":1791546994094,"changelog":"Pin the official CLI to 0.5.37, which removes preview upgrade prompts and requires a fresh signed-in full scan.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":16727,"sha256":"46fd5b7fbbbce4d4b28ae67d47342ad373ca455d5aac08142aff804e5422e452","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/growth-recipes.md","size":4643,"sha256":"bac0b408b0d7a247591a7af6ecae143c6c8b5532e32cf45aabe63ebb79f7bb94","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/product-analytics-operating-model.md","size":3968,"sha256":"a2f7ab1efcba13be090c0e1535fd7c0102322cbd556667dbe64e9be197300184","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/setup-auth.md","size":2413,"sha256":"a47ededaea8441fccd0e5e11fabde6342d12e93873a5c9232622cc6c4b641e5c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2391,"sha256":"f8d0ecf60aac48f5f1bc06b96524afef5b7f9659b68095f45402347d4a5dbe84","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1791549318275,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"064a4f33526d937c6719437cc42a02e91187ebd9cc2449e72044c7edea3ea78c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/064a4f33526d937c6719437cc42a02e91187ebd9cc2449e72044c7edea3ea78c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1791548507313},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":20,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1791549318275},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed product-analytics helper that uses a pinned external CLI, browser approval, and scoped analytics workflows; its sensitive behaviors are purpose-aligned and bounded by consent and verification guidance.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill may inspect the user's repo, modify instrumentation, use browser/detached auth, and read analytics data including sessions and replays; those are sensitive but proportionate for product analytics and paired with consent-based setup and verification rules.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill requires running `npx --yes @agent-analytics/cli@0.5.37`, which downloads and executes an external npm package; this is clearly disclosed, pinned to a version, and central to the skill's stated function.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are scoped to Agent Analytics workflows, prefer fixed CLI commands, discourage raw API/curl substitutes, require user-confirmed goals before durable context storage, and explicitly warn against overtracking, PII, secrets, git logs, and unsupported guesses.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"It stores CLI auth under `.openclaw/agent-analytics` in managed runtimes and can write compact product context through `context set`; both are disclosed, scoped to the analytics service, and include guidance not to commit credentials or store PII/secrets.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill purpose is product analytics setup and analysis, and the capabilities it requests fit that purpose: installing a tracker, reading funnels/events/sessions/replays, managing project context, and recommending growth actions.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable using the Agent Analytics npm CLI and granting browser-approved access to your analytics account. Before setup, confirm the project goal and event plan, review any tracker/code changes, keep `.openclaw/agent-analytics/config.json` out of git, and avoid storing PII, secrets, or temporary analysis notes in project context.","findings":"[AR2] expected: The cited phrase `without judging too early` appears in a Bullseye channel-brainstorming recipe, not as an instruction to suppress safety warnings or override refusals; it is not material anti-refusal behavior in context.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1791549318275}}}}}